{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/180473-wraith-arcanos-quiz","id":180473,"title":"Wraith Arcanos Quiz","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-25T23:39:37-07:00","id":180473,"title":"Wraith Arcanos Quiz","content":"A 5 question quiz to determine starting Arcanos...<br /> <br /> You cannot answer the same number for more than 3 questions. If you do, go back and change your answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Q: It's Halloween, and you really want to scare your roommate. How do you do it?<br /> <br /> 1. Lead him by the hand through a haunted house, right into all the scary stuff.<br /> 2. Pour a couple drinks, and have a little chat about what scares him the most.<br /> 3. Write something creepy on the bathroom mirror just before he takes a shower. While he's standing there reading it, quietly stand right behind him.<br /> 4. Take him to see a fortune teller. Give her a tip and tell him to make it a good one.<br /> 5. Hack his computer to make him think it's possessed.<br /> 6. Hide a music player under his bed set to play haunting music all night long.<br /> 7. Spy on him. Leave little notes everywhere. Make him worry about being watched. You know, because he is.<br /> 8. Scary masks. Scary masks are AWESOME.<br /> 9. You are the bump in the middle of the night.<br /> 10. Wouldn't it be hilarious if you turned the apartment into a haunted house while he was gone? I wonder if I could nail that chair to the ceiling...<br /> 11. There's a play showing at the theatre downtown. Everyone says it's nightmare fuel.<br /> 12. Get your friends together one night to try out this new book about hypnosis you want to try out. Little does he know the game is rigged...<br /> 13. Since you work at a collection firm, you could probably mail him some scary letters on company letterhead. Maybe you have a different idea about what's scary...<br /> <br /> Q: If you had to do something else for a living, what would you do?<br /> <br /> 1. I could be a wilderness guide!<br /> 2. Maybe a therapist, or a priest.<br /> 3. Work is secondary to the pleasures you can buy with it.<br /> 4. I could read palms, perhaps? Can I tell your fortune?<br /> 5. I like to work with my hands.<br /> 6. Oh, to be a musician!<br /> 7. A private eye.<br /> 8. A clothing designer!<br /> 9. Whatever lets me take my frustrations out...<br /> 10. An architect! I see so many possibilities...<br /> 11. An actor. Theatre, television, movies... doesn't matter!<br /> 12. I like to be in a position of power. High level management.<br /> 13. Banking, trading stock, economics... that's the stuff.<br /> <br /> Q: I wish...<br /> <br /> 1. ...I could fly!<br /> 2. ...I had telepathy, so I could really understand what made people tick.<br /> 3. ...I could feel this great all the time.<br /> 4. ...I could see the future.<br /> 5. ...I had all the things I want.<br /> 6. ...I were a famous musician, and then everyone could feel what I feel.<br /> 7. ...I could protect all the things that were important to me.<br /> 8. ...I could change my shape, and look however I wanted.<br /> 9. ...I had telekinesis, like the guys in that movie. that was awesome!<br /> 10. ...Nobody could tell me what to do!<br /> 11. ...I could actually go to that place in the fantasy books I read...<br /> 12. ...People would just do what I tell them.<br /> 13. ...I was filthy. stinking. RICH.<br /> <br /> Q: Who do you admire?<br /> <br /> 1. Marco Polo, Ferdinand Magellan, and Neil Armstrong.<br /> 2. I had a teacher in school that would always take the time to listen to my problems...<br /> 3. Allen Ginsberg, William S. Burroughs, and Jack Kerouac.<br /> 4. Nostradamus was amazing.<br /> 5. My dad. He could fix anything.<br /> 6. [Insert favorite musician here]<br /> 7. J. Edgar Hoover.<br /> 8. My plastic surgeon.<br /> 9. I don't have time for idols. Tools of the establishment.<br /> 10. Ever seen those paintings by Dali? Those were amazing.<br /> 11. [Insert favorite actor here]<br /> 12. The president.<br /> 13. Donald Trump.<br /> <br /> Q: What special talent do you have?<br /> <br /> 1. Here, take a look at my scout merit badges.<br /> 2. I am a good listener. I am always there for people who need me.<br /> 3. I am willing, to you know, GO places. Expand my consciousness.<br /> 4. I have a sixth sense, believe it or not.<br /> 5. I can take anything apart and put it back together again.<br /> 6. I can sing, and play an instrument.<br /> 7. I pay attention to things most people miss.<br /> 8. I am a social chameleon.<br /> 9. Check this out. I can break these boards with my BARE HANDS.<br /> 10. I am... creative. (Smiles fiendishly)<br /> 11. I am an accomplished actor.<br /> 12. I know how to make people do what I want.<br /> 13. Who needs talent when you have money?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Answer Key. 1.Argos 2.Castigate 3.Embody 4.Fatalism 5.Inhabit 6.Keening 7.Lifeweb 8.Moliate 9.Outrage 10.Pandemonium 11.Phantasm 12.Puppetry 13.Usury","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T01:17:23-07:00","id":180507,"title":"","content":"So, Castigate 3, Inhabit 1, Puppetry 1.<br /> <br /> Not sure that's quite how I'd map out if I just did it myself without the quiz. I mean, Castigate makes sense for me and all and I'd see myself as a Pardoner. I'd see myself with Argos over either of the others and probably Outrage or Pandemonium out of the nastier side of my temperament if not Argos 2.<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem with it is that it tends a bit focus a bit much on what the Guilds are oriented around (which is fine for the Arcanos that's your primary focus). But for a lot of them, even if I go back and move the Castigate answers to other questions, I kind of find myself not caring for any of the answers particularly much. For example I've spent a lot of times in the woods, and generally am pretty good at orienteering, but I don't necessarily want to be a wilderness guide and I've never been in a scouting organization to earn merit badges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T02:04:31-07:00","id":180537,"title":"","content":"Open to suggestions. =]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:51:44-07:00","id":181091,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I have any specific suggestions on a particular question of the set, but I think the answers are uneven. Some are incredibly specific (&quot;I wish I could fly&quot;), and others are incredibly broad (&quot;I wish I had all the things I want&quot;). The admiration question is like this as well. You have &quot;any musician&quot; vs. J. Edgar Hoover vs. specific people in your own life. Instead of getting at what it is about other people that the quiz taker admires, which understandable relates to Arcanoi selection, you get stuck with odd choices where you have to try to interpret the meaning of the answer. Do I take Hoover even if I don't admire him personally but I get that the point is that I admire that kind of approach to power, or do I pick my 6th grade teacher because I do admire her for her understanding; even if I admire Machiavelli well over either of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}